      "text": "To determine when Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will next be together tutoring in the lab, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of their working cycles. Here, Darren works every 3 school days, Wanda every 4 school days, Beatrice every 6 school days, and Chi every 7 school days. Therefore, we need to find the LCM of the numbers 3, 4, 6, and 7.\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorization of each number:\n\\[\n3 = 3\n\\]\n\\[\n4 = 2^2\n\\]\n\\[\n6 = 2 \\times 3\n\\]\n\\[\n7 = 7\n\\]\n\nThe LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in the factorizations:\n- The highest power of 2 is \\(2^2\\) (from 4).\n- The highest power of 3 is \\(3\\) (from 3 and 6).\n- The highest power of 7 is \\(7\\) (from 7).\n\nThus, the LCM is:\n\\[\n2^2 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 4 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 84\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will next be together tutoring in the lab in \\(\\boxed{84}\\) school days.",
